# 🔗 Product-Engine Consolidation Plan
## Connecting Orphaned Engine Pages to Product Structure

**Created:** 2024-12-19  
**Status:** 🎯 PLANNING - Ready for implementation

---

## 🎯 PROBLEM STATEMENT

**Current State:**
- ✅ Built `/products/oncology` with capability showcase
- ✅ Built `/products/r-d` with capability showcase  
- ✅ Built `/products/research` (presumably)
- ❌ Separate orphaned engine pages: `/products/oracle`, `/products/forge`, `/products/boltz`, `/products/command-center`
- ❌ `EngineRoom` component on homepage links to individual engine pages
- ❌ No clear connection between products and engines

**User Request:**
- Consolidate engines into product structure
- Connect engines to R&D product page (since engines power R&D)
- Update EngineRoom to route to R&D page instead of individual pages
- Maintain individual engine pages but make them accessible from R&D page

---

## 🏗️ PROPOSED ARCHITECTURE

### **Hierarchical Structure:**
```
PRODUCTS (Customer-Facing)
├── /products/oncology
│   └── Powered by: Oracle, Command Center
├── /products/r-d
│   ├── Capabilities (Target Discovery, Therapeutic Design, etc.)
│   └── AI ENGINES SECTION (NEW)
│       ├── Oracle Engine → /products/r-d/engines/oracle
│       ├── Forge Engine → /products/r-d/engines/forge
│       ├── Boltz Engine → /products/r-d/engines/boltz
│       └── Command Center → /products/r-d/engines/command-center
└── /products/research
    └── Powered by: Oracle, Command Center
```

### **Option 1: Engines as Sub-Sections on R&D Page (RECOMMENDED)**
- Add "AI Engines" tab/section to `/products/r-d`
- Show 4 engine cards with metrics
- Each card links to detailed engine page
- EngineRoom component links to `/products/r-d#engines`

### **Option 2: Engines as Sub-Routes**
- Create `/products/r-d/engines/[engineSlug]` routes
- Keep existing engine pages but move them under R&D
- EngineRoom links to `/products/r-d/engines/oracle` etc.

### **Option 3: Engines as Tabs on R&D Page**
- Add engines as additional tabs alongside existing RDTabs
- Each tab shows full engine details inline
- No separate pages needed

